@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB License Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to OSB and License Management works properly.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                         |
	| DXP Backup                             |
	| DXP Non-Production                     |
	| Portal Production                      |
	| Platinum Subscription                  |
	| Gold Subscription                      |
	| Limited Subscription                   |
	| Enterprise Search for DXP Cloud - Prod |
	| Commerce Subscription Production       |
	| Developer Services                     |
	| Analytics Cloud Basic                  |
	| Enterprise Search - Production         |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Generate new DXP license
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I click on the Generate New License button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Account                | Korone - ${staticProjectName}              | |
	| Product                | DXP Production                             | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}                 | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORONE                        |
	| Name            | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |
	When I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for the summary "Added Product Consumption" related to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" field "accountId" from the old value "" to the new value "${staticAccountId}" regarding "DXP Production" executed by "Amos Fong"

Scenario: Generate new portal license
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 portal project from koroneiki

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "Portal Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I click on the Generate New License button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Account                | Korone - ${staticProjectName}  | |
	| Product                | Portal Production              | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 6.2 EE                         | |
	| Type                   | Portal Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}     | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                      | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F              | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORONE                        |
	| Name            | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |
	When I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for the summary "Added Product Consumption" related to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" field "accountId" from the old value "" to the new value "${staticAccountId}" regarding "Portal Production" executed by "Amos Fong"

Scenario: Generate new detached license
	Testing the ability to generate a new detached license for a T4 project from koroneiki

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I click on the Generate New License button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Account                | Korone - ${staticProjectName}  | |
	| Product                | Portal Production              | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 6.2 EE                         | |
	| Type                   | Portal Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | Detached                       | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                      | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F              | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORONE                        |
	| Name            | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	When I generate static start dates
	And I generate static end dates
	Then I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticEndDates}   | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates} | |

